1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,600
Vendor comparisons usually end up in a spreadsheet that starts going stale the day it is made.

2
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:15,640
Prices change, plan limits move, integrations disappear, and a confident AI answer may cite a page it never saw.

3
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:23,160
VendorProof turns a messy procurement brief into a live evidence file with links that can be checked.

4
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,460
This run starts with a real buying brief.

5
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:31,540
Compare Intercom, Zendesk, and Crisp for a five-person support team.

6
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:37,740
The brief includes a monthly budget, required capabilities, and deal breakers.

7
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:40,300
It is not a chat question.

8
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:47,820
It is the same kind of request a small team would hand to an operations lead before spending money.

9
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:55,080
After the form is submitted, Gemini extracts no more than five checks that could change the decision.

10
00:00:56,300 --> 00:01:02,300
VendorProof then searches Google Web and Google News through SerpApi for each check.

11
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:06,460
The production path has no canned search result.

12
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:13,700
Every piece of evidence on the report comes from the live responses returned during this run.

13
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:17,540
Gemini proposes and evaluates the checks.

14
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:22,760
SerpApi supplies current search results.

15
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:30,600
A separate enforcement layer compares every citation with the exact URLs returned in this run.

16
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:35,460
If a URL was not observed, it cannot appear as evidence.

17
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:43,400
Xano stores the original brief and the complete report, so the browser never receives provider credentials.

18
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:47,360
This is a real result from the deployed app.

19
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:55,800
The evidence file has a decision state, a confidence label, an explanation, a next action, and a clickable source.

20
00:01:55,800 --> 00:02:03,120
When a search channel fails or a citation is missing, VendorProof does not fill the gap with a guess.

21
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:08,920
It downgrades the claim and can force the whole report into review or hold.

22
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:16,300
The Xano receipt shows snapshot forty-seven and the previous snapshot used for comparison.

23
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:22,540
Xano normalizes the brief, serializes writes for the same brief, and saves the full evidence JSON.

24
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:26,300
It also reports how many claims changed.

25
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:29,700
The comparison is no longer a disposable answer.

26
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:34,700
It has a history that another person can audit later.

27
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:38,740
The deployed version passed three hundred ninety-one tests, with branch-aware coverage above ninety-five percent.

28
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:46,620
Secret scanning and push protection are enabled.

29
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:51,500
An independent code review found no actionable regressions.

30
00:02:51,500 --> 00:03:02,740
The production smoke test completed the full Gemini, SerpApi, and Xano chain.

31
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:05,920
VendorProof replaces a stale comparison sheet with current research and honest uncertainty.

32
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:11,120
The live app and public source repository are available now.

33
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:13,700
Evidence before commitment.
